From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: djvalic <djvalic@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] file_manager: report files it can't write as read-only

Moonraker's file lists (server.files.get_directory, server.files.list,
the file change notifications) reported "permissions": "rw" for every
file in a root it may write to, whoever owns the file. A plugin folder
copied into /data/ad5x/plugins as root over SSH (root:root, 0755, files
0644) was listed as writable to Moonraker (user klipper), so Fluidd
opened its files for editing, and each save failed with "Destination
file exists and appears to be read-only" and a 500 that Fluidd doesn't
show (issue #96, fluidd-core/fluidd#2040).

get_path_info() now lowers "rw" to "r" when the process can't write the
item (os.access W_OK with the effective ids, as the upload check does):
a file needs write access to itself and to the folder that holds it, a
folder to itself. An upload is moved over the file from the temp folder
(TMPDIR, on the data partition on Kiln OS): the rename needs the folder,
the copy shutil.move() falls back to needs the file, and a delete or a
rename needs the folder, so "rw" means all of these work; a file that
only one of the two ways could replace is listed "r" as well. A folder
is "r" when nothing can be created in it.

The rules before stay: read-only roots, linked files, .git and the
reserved paths (the update manager's git_repo folders without a
.writeable file) give what they gave, and nothing that was "r" or ""
becomes "rw". The roots themselves (root_info, server.files.roots)
still follow full_access_roots. The listings check each folder once
(folder_access), so a listing costs one access() per entry and one per
folder.

Fluidd shows a file listed "r" with a lock and doesn't offer to save it.

Upstream: not submitted (AD5X open OS)
